                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Essentials of Clinical Pharmacology" is an English-taught graduate course designed for students in clinical-related disciplines such as medicine and pharmacy. Centered on the mechanisms of drug action, pharmacokinetic processes (ADME), efficacy evaluation, and clinical applications, the curriculum spans critical modules including drug development, individual variability, adverse reactions, and clinical trials. Emphasizing the integration of theoretical knowledge with practical applications, the course employs case studies, group discussions, and seminars to enhance students' analytical and problem-solving skills in pharmacotherapy. It aims to equip learners with a robust foundation for future endeavors in clinical drug research, pharmacological evaluation, and translational medicine.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
